        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4784,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1949,
        "paragraph_id": "298FC9DD",
        "text": "The advection-diffusion equation for suspended sediment is the basis for the sediment transport computations in XBeach. The partial differential equation to solve is:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 98491,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4788,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1953,
        "paragraph_id": "1970AB0B",
        "text": "Here C is the depth-averaged concentration, Ceq the equilibrium concentration, Ts a typical timescale proportional to water depth divided by fall velocity. As is often done to increase robustness, we treat the erosion term explicitly but taking an implicit scheme for the sedimentation term:"
      },
      {
